                <p class="clarity-eyebrow"><span>01</span> How exposure really happens</p>
                <h2 id="exposure-title">They may not need to hack you.</h2>
                <p class="clarity-lede">The most consequential exposure rarely announces itself as a cyberattack. It sits inside the ordinary digital life you already have: a personal email used for work, an old recovery path, a device once shared, an identity repeated across accounts, a permission that still survives.</p>
            </div>
            <p class="exposure-intro-note">One item may look harmless. The combination is what matters.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
