<section class="clarity-section" id="method" data-field="sand" aria-labelledby="method-title">
    <div class="clarity-wrap method-grid">
        <div class="method-intro">
            <p class="clarity-eyebrow"><span>02</span> What Toza does</p>
            <h2 id="method-title">Find the whole path. Then act.</h2>
            <p>I developed a complete personal-hardening method for high-risk personal situations.</p>
            <p class="method-basis">It combines current government security standards, guidance for high-risk individuals, platform-specific protections and twenty years of field experience in one disciplined sequence.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
            <div class="method-rows">
                <article class="method-row"><span>01</span><h3>Map</h3><p>I reconstruct how the phone, computer, identities, apps, public trails, recovery paths and shared access fit together. If I find urgent exposure, I begin containing it during the assessment.</p></article>
                <article class="method-row"><span>02</span><h3>Close and harden</h3><p>I carry the work through Personal Shield. I harden the phone, computer, identities and apps, replace risky core accounts where necessary, move essential access and recovery, and configure two physical security keys.</p></article>
                <article class="method-row"><span>03</span><h3>Verify</h3><p>I test every completed change, finish the hardening checklist, train you and provide a private dated record.</p></article>
            </div>
            <p class="method-close">The assessment begins the method. Personal Shield carries the full hardening through to completion. A typical Personal Shield engagement requires one or two working days, depending on the volume of data and apps, the complexity of the account relationships and the threat model.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

